{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":15274,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"Hydration of NAD(P)H to NAD(P)HX, which inhibits several dehydrogenases, is corrected by an ATP-dependent dehydratase and an epimerase. The ATP-dependent dehydratase has been identified as the product of the vertebrate Carkd (carbohydrate kinase domain) gene [[cite:PUB00073185],[cite:PUB00100876]]. Variants of this enzyme leads to deficient NADHX repair mitochondrial dysfunction in humans, associated with a lethal neurometabolic disorder in early childhood [[cite:PUB00100876]]. In E. coli, it is found as the C-terminal domain of a bifunctional enzyme (YjeF) that also includes the epimerase and uses ADP instead of ATP [[cite:PUB00060794]]. These enzymes are widespread in eukaryotes, prokaryotes, and archaea.","domain_architectures":88,"interpro_id":"IPR000631","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":22644,"name":"NAD(P)H-hydrate dehydratase","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF01256","proteins":22302,"proteomes":19898,"short_name":"Carb_kinase","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF01256","structures":37,"taxa":32358,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"SEEDED","local_source":"source/data/families/PF01256.yaml","record":{"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":15274,"domain_architectures":88,"matches":22644,"proteins":22302,"proteomes":19898,"structures":37,"taxa":32358},"curation_status":"SEEDED","description":"Hydration of NAD(P)H to NAD(P)HX, which